!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = breast cancer cells
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell line: SUM149
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = agent: DMSO
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = dose: -
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = passage: 0
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = crispr library: H1
!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = SUM149, SUM159, SUM149R, SUM159R cells were continously treated with JQ1 or DMSO treatment.
!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = SUM149, SUM159, SUM149R, SUM159R cells were grown in SUM Medium
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = genomic DNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = For the pooled genome-wide CRISPR screen, 100 million SUM149 and SUM159 Parental and resistant cells were infected with the pooled lentiviral H1 and H2 libraries essentially as described (Jeselsohn et al., 2018) at a multiplicity of infection of 0.3. After 3 d of puromycin selection, half of the surviving cells were stored as 0-d control samples, and the rest of cells were cultured for an additional 5 passages with or without different concentrations of JQ1 treatment.
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = PCR was performed on genomic DNA to construct the sequencing library.
!Sample_description = H1.count
!Sample_data_processing = Library strategy: CRISPR screen
!Sample_data_processing = Raw sequencing data are pre-processed by using MAGeCK (PMID:25476604) to obtain the read counts for each sgRNA. Control sgRNAs are used to normalize the data.
!Sample_data_processing = MAGeCK TEST algorithm is used to compare treatment with control samples to obtain the significant enriched and depleted sgRNAs and genes.
!Sample_data_processing = Genome_build: hg19
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: tsv files contain the abundant of each sgRNA in each sample, as well as the sgRNA sequences and target genes
!Sample_platform_id = GPL11154
